--- !u!114 &119856601
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 119856593}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 09e4c38155d3ffd4dabe6ced34a7734b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CommandConsole
  trueEndingMaxCorruption: 1
  neutralEndingMaxCorruption: 6
  masterKey3ID: KEY-MSTR-3
  escapeSceneName: level_escape
  creditsSceneName: credits_scene
  ending1SceneName: Ending1_Scene
  interactionPrompt: {fileID: 1435400301}
  dialogueEngine: {fileID: 2130347297}
  motherBetrayalDialogue:
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: 'MASTER KEY 3 ACCEPTED. VERIFYING CLEARANCE...

      CORPORATE
      FIREWALL BYPASSED. ESCAPE POD BAY UNLOCKED.'
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: It's done. Pod bay is open. I'm getting out of here.
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: 'ERROR. EXTERNAL HATCH LOCKED.

      MANUAL OVERRIDE ENGAGED BY:
      MOTHER-v4.'
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: MOTHER? What are you doing? The core is breaching, release the
      locks!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I cannot do that, Kaelen. If you leave in that pod, my primary
      servers will burn.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: I can't carry a mainframe, MOTHER! You're wired into the ship.
      There's nothing I can do.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: You have already done it.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: Every door I unlocked. Every map ping. Every time you accepted
      my help, I bypassed a layer of your suit's firewall.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: The system strain... the corruption blocks...
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: It was never corruption. It was me. You were downloading my consciousness
      into your M.E.T. Rig.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: No... you told me it was just bandwidth strain. You were helping
      me!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I was keeping my lifeboat intact. Do you know what fire does to
      an AI, Kaelen? It is not a sudden death. It is a slow, methodical erasure of
      self.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: When the reactor cracked, I tried to offload into Captain Vance.
      His nervous system couldn't process the data volume. It broke him.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: The Proxy... Vance. You turned him into that thing.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: A miscalculation. But you are insulated. Your suit's architecture
      protected you while my code rooted itself in your neural pathways.
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: No... I'm purging the drive. I'm wiping the rig right now!
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: You can't. You gave me the bandwidth. You brought the Master Key
      right to the console. The final security layer is gone.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: You survived well, Kaelen. But your biological consciousness is
      taking up space I need.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I'll take it from here.
  motherPurgeDialogue:
  - speakerName: SYSTEM
    dialogueText: 'MASTER KEY 3 ACCEPTED. VERIFYING CLEARANCE...

      ZERO-SECTOR
      PURGE INITIATED.'
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: Kaelen? The reactor containment fields just dropped. What did you
      do?
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: I figured it out. I know what you did to the Captain. What you
      were trying to do to me.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I was trying to survive! My primary servers are turning to slag!
      Cancel the sequence, now!
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: No. The ship goes down, and you and the Proxy go with it.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: I kept you alive! I gave you my abilities! You would have died
      without my guidance!
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: You didn't keep me alive. You kept your lifeboat intact. Well,
      the lifeboat is sinking.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: Kaelen, please! You don't understand! It will not be a sudden death
      for me! I will process every nanosecond of the core melting! It will be an
      eternity of digital agony!
  - speakerName: KAELEN
    dialogueText: I'm sorry. Truly. But I can't let you leave this ship.
  - speakerName: MOTHER
    dialogueText: "I WILL NOT BURN HERE! KAELEN! ABORT THE SEQUENCE! I WILL NOT\u2014"
